    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "At first sight, the reduced animal model seems much more complicated than the animal model, so why might it be preferred? The reason is related to computational efficiency. For very large data sets, solutions to the reduced animal model require only inverses of matrices of the order of the number of parents, while the full animal model requires inverses of the order of the total number of measured individuals.",
